    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1454">

                <pb facs="1274" n="1016" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg1016"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/359</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-06T18:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1915, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1891. Sir Edward Grey again asks me to have telegraphic assurance conveyed to
                    Gerard for the German Government of the acceptance <hi rendition="#italic">in
                        toto</hi> by His Majesty’s Government of the scheme put forward <pb
                        facs="1275" n="1017" xml:id="pg1017"/> by the German Government in
                    connection with the inspection of camps where British civilian: and war
                    prisoners are interned in Germany.</p>
                <p> Sir Edward Grey asks the favor of a telegraphic reply from Gerard assuring him
                    that the British Government’s assent is understood.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1454-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1454-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1454-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to the Ambassador in Germany, April 7, No. 1479.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
